      "answer": "The customer whose issue started after the 2026-02-20 taxonomy rollout is BlueHarbor Logistics. The proof plan proposed to get them comfortable with renewal is a 7-10 business day proof involving updating index weighting and adding a mapping layer to translate new taxonomy terms to old query terms for the top 20 saved searches. The acceptance criteria include achieving a top-5 correct hit rate of at least 80%, no regression in suppression logic, and incident correlation latency under 200ms. The plan includes a 90-day fixed-price professional services engagement at $48k (with a 30% discount if Orchestrator expansion is signed concurrently) to implement the tuning, mapping layer, and run the proof. There is also a conditional credit on renewal if the proof does not meet the agreed metrics, along with a detailed timeline and responsibilities for data provision, testing, validation, and rollout [art_0bccc580184e, art_bd3560dfe194].",
