      "answer": "The SCIM fields conflicting at Aureum were \"department\" and \"businessUnit.\" Merchant Services used \"businessUnit=merchant\" while Payments Ops used \"department=payments,\" causing ingestion normalization failures and routing mismatches in the Rules Engine. Jin proposed a fast fix to add a preprocessing rule in Signal Ingest to map \"businessUnit\" to \"department\" (or vice versa) and publish a normalized field for the correlator. This fix is a configuration-only change, hot-reloadable, and does not require changes to Okta flows or appliance restarts during settlement windows, enabling a quick resolution without waiting for Okta change control. [art_79f625aafa16] [art_545110f843dc]",
